

| ### This feature is in beta
| 
| To use this feature, pass in a header including the LD-API-Version key with value set to beta. Use this header with each call. To learn more, read Beta resources https://launchdarkly.com/docs/api#beta-resources.
| 
| Resources that are in beta are still undergoing testing and development. They may change without notice, including becoming backwards incompatible.
| The views API allows you to create, retrieve, and edit views, and link other resources to views.

A view is a resource in LaunchDarkly that you can use to logically group other resources within a project, such as flags or segments. For example, views let you restrict access to sets of flags, so that members of your organization can focus on just the flags they work with.

To learn more, read Views https://launchdarkly.com/docs/home/account/views.

Usage:
  ldcli views-beta [command]

Available Commands:
  create                Create view
  delete                Delete view
  get                   Get view
  link-resource         Link resource
  list                  List views
  list-linked           Get linked views for a given resource
  list-linked-resources Get linked resources
  unlink-resource       Unlink resource
  update                Update view

Global flags:
  -h, --help                  Get help about any command
      --access-token string   LaunchDarkly access token with write-level access
      --analytics-opt-out     Opt out of analytics tracking
      --base-uri string       LaunchDarkly base URI (default "https://app.launchdarkly.com")
      --fields strings        Comma-separated list of top-level fields to include in JSON output (e.g., --fields key,name,kind)
      --json                  Output JSON format (shorthand for --output json)
  -o, --output string         Output format: json, plaintext, or markdown (default: plaintext in a terminal, json otherwise) (default "json")

Use "ldcli views-beta [command] --help" for more information about a command.
